Subject: Include <signal.h> before defining SYS_SECCOMP (glibc >= 2.42)
Upstream: No
Origin: Wolfi Community Packages

Recent glibc declares SYS_SECCOMP as an enumerator in
<bits/siginfo-consts.h>. Chromium's linux_seccomp.h defines
SYS_SECCOMP as the macro 1 when it is not yet defined, so if <signal.h>
is included afterwards the glibc declaration expands to "1 = 1" and
the sandbox fails to build. Including <signal.h> first lets glibc
define SYS_SECCOMP and the #ifndef guard skip the fallback.

--- a/src/3rdparty/chromium/sandbox/linux/system_headers/linux_seccomp.h	2026-10-14 01:28:57.753458132 +0000
+++ b/src/3rdparty/chromium/sandbox/linux/system_headers/linux_seccomp.h	2026-10-14 01:28:57.804866640 +0000
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
 #ifndef SANDBOX_LINUX_SYSTEM_HEADERS_LINUX_SECCOMP_H_
 #define SANDBOX_LINUX_SYSTEM_HEADERS_LINUX_SECCOMP_H_
 
+#include <signal.h>
 #include <stdint.h>
 
 #include "build/build_config.h"
